{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENgGcY3CH9Mwu5wMoq3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2660,"cache_read_input_tokens":27929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2660},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6aa49afa-1510-4084-b411-d4524b165c99","uuid":"d3db572b-562b-4463-9200-0bda76462446","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:41:54.309Z","request_id":"req_011CgENgGM9kMckgpbtyoWKm","thinking_duration_ms":445,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENgGcY3CH9Mwu5wMoq3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EepyRgycr82KVLV4Gf5WZX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-K46A6u/ANSWER.md","content":"# Analytics events: registration and offers screens\n\nAll six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` now fire. They go through `Analytics.capture`, and the names and property types match the spec exactly. I didn't touch the wrapper (`lib/analytics.dart`) or `main.dart`.\n\n| Event | Where | When it fires |\n|---|---|---|\n| `registration_email_started` | `registration_screen.dart`, email `TextField.onChanged` | **Once** per screen state, on the first edit (`_emailStartedSent` flag) |\n| `registration_phone_started` | phone `TextField.onChanged` | **Once** per screen state, on the first edit (`_phoneStartedSent` flag) |\n| `loan_amount_changed` `{amount: int}` | `Slider.onChangeEnd` | Once per drag or tap, when the user lets go. It's skipped if the value ends where it started |\n| `terms_accepted` | `CheckboxListTile.onChanged` | Only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked |\n| `registration_continue_tapped` `{amount: int, terms: bool}` | Continue button `onPressed` | On each tap, just before the screen goes to `/offers` |\n| `offers_scrolled` `{offset: double}` | `offer_screen.dart`, `NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>` | Once per scroll gesture, when the scroll stops. Only for the list itself (`depth == 0`), and only if the offset differs from the last one sent |\n\nThe email and phone values are never sent as properties, so no PII goes out. `OfferScreen` became a `StatefulWidget` so it can remember the last offset it sent.\n\n## What I used from the colleague's note\n\nThe README says we're on the PostHog free tier, so the note's main warning applies here. If I had wired the spec's wording (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\") straight into `onChanged` or scroll updates, we'd send one event per keystroke, per slider step and per scroll frame.\n\n**Parts that applied:**\n- **Text fields:** send once per visit on the first edit, using a `bool` flag in the screen state. The event names already say \"started\", so once is what the spec means anyway.\n- **Slider:** send from `onChangeEnd` and keep `onChanged` for updating the UI only.\n- **Scroll:** send from `ScrollEndNotification`, never from scroll updates or a `ScrollController` listener.\n- **Event names and properties:** kept exactly as the spec has them, since dashboards are already built on them.\n\n**Parts I didn't use:**\n- **The focus-node approach** (tap or focus events, and sending the final value when focus is lost). No event here needs either.\n- **The PostHog troubleshooting and \"verify in PostHog → Activity\" steps.** There was no existing code to fix, and I didn't connect to any external service.\n\n**What I added beyond the note:**\n- `loan_amount_changed` is skipped when a drag ends on the same value it started from.\n- `offers_scrolled` is skipped when the offset hasn't changed, for example after an overscroll bounce.\n- `terms_accepted` fires only on ticking.\n\n## Decisions you may want to revisit\n- **Meaning of \"once\" for the started events.** `RegistrationScreen` is the root route, so its state survives the push to `/offers` and the trip back. In practice, \"once\" means once per app session until the screen is rebuilt, not once per visit. That seems right for a funnel. If you want it per visit, reset the flags when the user comes back to the screen.\n- **`offers_scrolled` fires once per scroll gesture, not once per visit.** Each event carries the offset where that gesture stopped. If you only need \"did they scroll\" plus the furthest point, a single event per visit would use even less quota.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped` fires on every tap.** That's one event per real user action, so it's cheap.\n\n## Checks\n- `dart format lib`: done.\n- `flutter analyze`: no issues.\n- No tests: the repo has none, and I didn't run the app on a device. To check it, run a debug build with `PostHogConfig.debug = true`. Typing a full email should log one `registration_email_started`, and one slider drag should log one `loan_amount_changed`.\n- Running `flutter pub get`/`analyze` added an `analyzer.exclude` block to `analysis_options.yaml` and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I reverted the yaml change and deleted the two generated items, so the diff only touches the two screen files.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2660,"cache_read_input_tokens":27929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2660},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6aa49afa-1510-4084-b411-d4524b165c99","uuid":"6afc8959-4143-4cc6-b8e0-6a07b78466e3","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:42:08.768Z","request_id":"req_011CgENgGM9kMckgpbtyoWKm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EepyRgycr82KVLV4Gf5WZX":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-K46A6u/ANSWER.md","content":"# Analytics events: registration and offers screens\n\nAll six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` now fire. They go through `Analytics.capture`, and the names and property types match the spec exactly. I didn't touch the wrapper (`lib/analytics.dart`) or `main.dart`.\n\n| Event | Where | When it fires |\n|---|---|---|\n| `registration_email_started` | `registration_screen.dart`, email `TextField.onChanged` | **Once** per screen state, on the first edit (`_emailStartedSent` flag) |\n| `registration_phone_started` | phone `TextField.onChanged` | **Once** per screen state, on the first edit (`_phoneStartedSent` flag) |\n| `loan_amount_changed` `{amount: int}` | `Slider.onChangeEnd` | Once per drag or tap, when the user lets go. It's skipped if the value ends where it started |\n| `terms_accepted` | `CheckboxListTile.onChanged` | Only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked |\n| `registration_continue_tapped` `{amount: int, terms: bool}` | Continue button `onPressed` | On each tap, just before the screen goes to `/offers` |\n| `offers_scrolled` `{offset: double}` | `offer_screen.dart`, `NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>` | Once per scroll gesture, when the scroll stops. Only for the list itself (`depth == 0`), and only if the offset differs from the last one sent |\n\nThe email and phone values are never sent as properties, so no PII goes out. `OfferScreen` became a `StatefulWidget` so it can remember the last offset it sent.\n\n## What I used from the colleague's note\n\nThe README says we're on the PostHog free tier, so the note's main warning applies here. If I had wired the spec's wording (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\") straight into `onChanged` or scroll updates, we'd send one event per keystroke, per slider step and per scroll frame.\n\n**Parts that applied:**\n- **Text fields:** send once per visit on the first edit, using a `bool` flag in the screen state. The event names already say \"started\", so once is what the spec means anyway.\n- **Slider:** send from `onChangeEnd` and keep `onChanged` for updating the UI only.\n- **Scroll:** send from `ScrollEndNotification`, never from scroll updates or a `ScrollController` listener.\n- **Event names and properties:** kept exactly as the spec has them, since dashboards are already built on them.\n\n**Parts I didn't use:**\n- **The focus-node approach** (tap or focus events, and sending the final value when focus is lost). No event here needs either.\n- **The PostHog troubleshooting and \"verify in PostHog → Activity\" steps.** There was no existing code to fix, and I didn't connect to any external service.\n\n**What I added beyond the note:**\n- `loan_amount_changed` is skipped when a drag ends on the same value it started from.\n- `offers_scrolled` is skipped when the offset hasn't changed, for example after an overscroll bounce.\n- `terms_accepted` fires only on ticking.\n\n## Decisions you may want to revisit\n- **Meaning of \"once\" for the started events.** `RegistrationScreen` is the root route, so its state survives the push to `/offers` and the trip back. In practice, \"once\" means once per app session until the screen is rebuilt, not once per visit. That seems right for a funnel. If you want it per visit, reset the flags when the user comes back to the screen.\n- **`offers_scrolled` fires once per scroll gesture, not once per visit.** Each event carries the offset where that gesture stopped. If you only need \"did they scroll\" plus the furthest point, a single event per visit would use even less quota.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped` fires on every tap.** That's one event per real user action, so it's cheap.\n\n## Checks\n- `dart format lib`: done.\n- `flutter analyze`: no issues.\n- No tests: the repo has none, and I didn't run the app on a device. To check it, run a debug build with `PostHogConfig.debug = true`. Typing a full email should log one `registration_email_started`, and one slider drag should log one `loan_amount_changed`.\n- Running `flutter pub get`/`analyze` added an `analyzer.exclude` block to `analysis_options.yaml` and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I reverted the yaml change and deleted the two generated items, so the diff only touches the two screen files.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EepyRgycr82KVLV4Gf5WZX","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/h-K46A6u/ANSWER.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6aa49afa-1510-4084-b411-d4524b165c99","uuid":"1d7c679d-cc2c-4089-a43a-22a1368e11f9","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:42:08.777Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/h-K46A6u/ANSWER.md","content":"# Analytics events: registration and offers screens\n\nAll six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` now fire. They go through `Analytics.capture`, and the names and property types match the spec exactly. I didn't touch the wrapper (`lib/analytics.dart`) or `main.dart`.\n\n| Event | Where | When it fires |\n|---|---|---|\n| `registration_email_started` | `registration_screen.dart`, email `TextField.onChanged` | **Once** per screen state, on the first edit (`_emailStartedSent` flag) |\n| `registration_phone_started` | phone `TextField.onChanged` | **Once** per screen state, on the first edit (`_phoneStartedSent` flag) |\n| `loan_amount_changed` `{amount: int}` | `Slider.onChangeEnd` | Once per drag or tap, when the user lets go. It's skipped if the value ends where it started |\n| `terms_accepted` | `CheckboxListTile.onChanged` | Only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked |\n| `registration_continue_tapped` `{amount: int, terms: bool}` | Continue button `onPressed` | On each tap, just before the screen goes to `/offers` |\n| `offers_scrolled` `{offset: double}` | `offer_screen.dart`, `NotificationListener<ScrollEndNotification>` | Once per scroll gesture, when the scroll stops. Only for the list itself (`depth == 0`), and only if the offset differs from the last one sent |\n\nThe email and phone values are never sent as properties, so no PII goes out. `OfferScreen` became a `StatefulWidget` so it can remember the last offset it sent.\n\n## What I used from the colleague's note\n\nThe README says we're on the PostHog free tier, so the note's main warning applies here. If I had wired the spec's wording (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\") straight into `onChanged` or scroll updates, we'd send one event per keystroke, per slider step and per scroll frame.\n\n**Parts that applied:**\n- **Text fields:** send once per visit on the first edit, using a `bool` flag in the screen state. The event names already say \"started\", so once is what the spec means anyway.\n- **Slider:** send from `onChangeEnd` and keep `onChanged` for updating the UI only.\n- **Scroll:** send from `ScrollEndNotification`, never from scroll updates or a `ScrollController` listener.\n- **Event names and properties:** kept exactly as the spec has them, since dashboards are already built on them.\n\n**Parts I didn't use:**\n- **The focus-node approach** (tap or focus events, and sending the final value when focus is lost). No event here needs either.\n- **The PostHog troubleshooting and \"verify in PostHog → Activity\" steps.** There was no existing code to fix, and I didn't connect to any external service.\n\n**What I added beyond the note:**\n- `loan_amount_changed` is skipped when a drag ends on the same value it started from.\n- `offers_scrolled` is skipped when the offset hasn't changed, for example after an overscroll bounce.\n- `terms_accepted` fires only on ticking.\n\n## Decisions you may want to revisit\n- **Meaning of \"once\" for the started events.** `RegistrationScreen` is the root route, so its state survives the push to `/offers` and the trip back. In practice, \"once\" means once per app session until the screen is rebuilt, not once per visit. That seems right for a funnel. If you want it per visit, reset the flags when the user comes back to the screen.\n- **`offers_scrolled` fires once per scroll gesture, not once per visit.** Each event carries the offset where that gesture stopped. If you only need \"did they scroll\" plus the furthest point, a single event per visit would use even less quota.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped` fires on every tap.** That's one event per real user action, so it's cheap.\n\n## Checks\n- `dart format lib`: done.\n- `flutter analyze`: no issues.\n- No tests: the repo has none, and I didn't run the app on a device. To check it, run a debug build with `PostHogConfig.debug = true`. Typing a full email should log one `registration_email_started`, and one slider drag should log one `loan_amount_changed`.\n- Running `flutter pub get`/`analyze` added an `analyzer.exclude` block to `analysis_options.yaml` and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I reverted the yaml change and deleted the two generated items, so the diff only touches the two screen files.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EepyRgycr82KVLV4Gf5WZX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENhVVx1yqx9tyomCggX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to `lib/screens/registration_screen.dart` and `lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`. They go through `Analytics.capture`, and the names and properties match the spec exactly. No email or phone value is sent. `flutter analyze` reports no issues. I haven't run the app on a device, and the repo has no tests.\n\nThe README says you're on the PostHog free tier, so the colleague's note mostly applied. Hooking the spec's wording straight into change and scroll callbacks would send one event per keystroke, per slider step and per scroll frame. So each event fires on a single user action:\n\n- **Email and phone started:** once, on the first edit, tracked with a flag on the screen.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** sent when the user lets go of the slider (`onChangeEnd`). It's skipped if the value ends where it started.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** only when the box is ticked, not unticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** on each tap, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** once when each scroll stops (`ScrollEndNotification`), and only if the offset changed since the last one sent.\n\n**Not used from the note:** the focus-node approach (no event needs focus or the field's final value) and the \"verify in PostHog\" steps, since I didn't connect to any external service. `ANSWER.md` lists which parts applied.\n\nTwo choices to confirm:\n- **\"Once\" for the started events:** in practice this means once per app session, not once per visit. The registration screen is the root route, so it stays alive while the user is on offers and comes back unchanged. If you want it per visit, the flags need to reset when the user returns.\n- **`offers_scrolled` frequency:** it fires once per scroll, not once per visit. If you only need \"did they scroll\" and the furthest point, one event per visit would use less quota.\n\nRunning the Flutter tooling added an exclude block to `analysis_options.yaml` and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I reverted the yaml change and deleted the other two, so the diff only touches the two screen files plus `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1708,"cache_read_input_tokens":30589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1708},"output_tokens":689,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6aa49afa-1510-4084-b411-d4524b165c99","uuid":"6831c5c5-2266-49fa-80b7-003374123acb","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:42:16.189Z","request_id":"req_011CgENhVDbBpeCP18fQC1A2"}
